
- The quiescent power consumption of the LDO should be no larger than 5000 μW.
- The DC loop gain of the LDO should be at least 25 dB.
- The loop gain-bandwidth product (GBW) should be at least 10000 Hz.
- The phase margin should be at least 30 degrees.
- The power supply rejection ratio (PSRR) at DC should be at least 10 dB.
- The line regulation (LNR) should be no larger than 1.0 V/V per volt of supply change.
- The load regulation (LR) should be no larger than 20 per ampere of load change.
- The output voltage offset (vos) at maximum load should be no larger than 0.3 V.
- The transient undershoot under a 10 μA to 10 mA load step should be no larger than 1.2 V.
- The transient overshoot under a 10 mA to 10 μA load step should be no larger than 1.2 V.
